"major-12|cups-13":"Deep feeling, held in stillness. You or someone close is willing to wait and listen rather than push. Single, your sensitivity gives you an unusual view of what a partner needs. Partnered, hold space for your person's feelings without trying to fix them, and let understanding form.",
"major-12|cups-14":"Calm and willing surrender to the moment. Someone, maybe you, does not need to control how love unfolds. Single, steady maturity means being at peace with waiting well. Partnered, listen fully before you respond, and be willing to see a conflict from your partner's side.",
"major-12|swords-01":"A new way of seeing things may arrive while you hold still. Let a fresh thought about your love life sink in before acting on it. If partnered, look at a familiar issue from their side. If single, a shift in perspective may change what you are looking for.",
"major-12|swords-02":"Willingly pausing may be the way past a stalemate. Stop arguing your own view for a moment and try on theirs. If single, hold off on choosing between two options and see what you learn from staying still. The answer may appear once you stop forcing it.",
"major-12|swords-03":"A hurt asks for a pause, not a reaction. Let yourself feel it without acting on it, and try to see the situation from a wider angle. If single, letting the ache settle may show you what you truly need. If partnered, give each other patient space.",
"major-12|swords-04":"A double dose of stillness is here. Rest, do not push, and let the relationship or your heart breathe. If partnered, agree to leave a decision for now. If single, an unhurried stretch alone can be a fresh vantage point. Nothing is lost by pausing.",
"major-12|swords-05":"Stepping out of a fight to see it from the other side is a gift. Set down the need to win and ask what they experienced. If single, notice where you have been defending instead of connecting. A willing pause can turn a tug of war into a conversation.",
"major-12|swords-06":"Moving on often begins with looking back from a new angle. Take time to understand what the past taught you before you leave it. If partnered, consider what a calmer path might need from each of you. If single, let the transition take as long as it takes.",
"major-12|swords-07":"Pausing might reveal what is being avoided. Look at your situation from the outside: is anything being kept quiet? If it is you, consider telling the truth. If single, take your time before trusting, and let actions add up. Patience protects you from clever stories.",
"major-12|swords-08":"You may be stuck in one view of things. Shift your angle on purpose: what would a kind friend say about your situation? If partnered, imagine their perspective. If single, question the rule that says you cannot be loved. A changed view can loosen the binding.",
