"major-12|swords-10":"An ending is complete, and surrender is easier than resistance. Let yourself stop trying to fix what is done. Rest in the pause and look at what you learned from a wider angle. If single, this stillness is a doorway to something new, when you feel ready.",
"major-12|swords-11":"A willing pause and a curious question make a good pair. Ask about something you have never understood in someone, then hold still and listen. If single, watch before you leap into a new connection. If partnered, take their side of a familiar matter as a thought experiment.",
"major-12|swords-12":"Speed meets stillness, and stillness has a point. If you feel like charging in with your opinion, hold it for a day. If a partner is pushing hard, ask for a pause. If single, let interest grow slowly rather than racing to a label.",
"major-12|swords-13":"Clear sight grows when you are willing to see from another side. Honestly consider the other person's view, then state your own plainly. If single, take time to look at your patterns without excuses or comfort stories. Both honesty and patience help you choose well.",
"major-12|swords-14":"Principle and patience are a strong pairing. Before you rule on a disagreement, spend time seeing it from their side. If partnered, explain your reasoning warmly and stay open. If single, look for someone whose judgment is thoughtful and unhurried, and offer the same.",
"major-12|pentacles-01":"Pause before rushing into something new, and look at it from another angle. What would this beginning look like through the other person's eyes? If you are single, delay a first move for a day and see what that reveals. If you are partnered, a short break in routine can bring fresh perspective.",
