"cups-07|cups-10":"A cloud of possibilities meets a picture of lasting family life. If you are single, ask which of your dreams includes real belonging. If together, dreams of elsewhere can be weighed against the home you have made. Substance usually outlasts novelty.",
"cups-07|cups-11":"A tender message arrives amid a swirl of fantasies. If you are single, respond to the real person who wrote to you, not to the story you are building. If together, tell your partner something small and true. Daydreams are lovely, and a message you can answer is better.",
"cups-07|cups-12":"A romantic invitation comes into a mind full of alternatives. If you are single, go on the date and pay attention to how you actually feel, rather than to what you imagined. If together, enjoy the gesture and ask whether the charm is also consistent. Let reality add its own detail.",
"cups-07|cups-13":"A wise, feeling person helps you sort real from imagined. If you are single, talk with a trusted friend who can reflect your patterns back. If together, let your partner know which fantasies you are holding. Being understood helps you choose.",
"cups-07|cups-14":"Many dreams, one sensible person. If you are single, pick a partner for character, not for the most vivid fantasy. If together, bring an honest, grown-up view to what you are hoping for. Structure does not kill romance; it gives it somewhere to live.",
"cups-08|cups-09":"Leaving and contentment are in the same frame, and the question is which one wins. If you are single, walking away from the wrong thing may lead to satisfaction on your own. If together, contentment might be nearer than you think, so ask before packing.",
"cups-08|cups-10":"Turning away from one life while longing for another: belonging is what you seek. If you are single, leaving an unrewarding situation can make room for a community that fits. If together, consider whether you are leaving the relationship or only one of its patterns. Home is worth building.",
